    "Description": "Red Hat JBoss Enterprise Application Platform 7 is a platform for Java applications based on the WildFly application runtime. This release of Red Hat JBoss Enterprise Application Platform 7.1.16 serves as a replacement for Red Hat JBoss Enterprise Application Platform 7.1.15, and includes bug fixes and enhancements. See the Red Hat JBoss Enterprise Application Platform 7.1.16 Release Notes for information about the most significant bug fixes and enhancements included in this release.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* mchange-commons-java: mchange-commons-java: Arbitrary code execution via\nJNDI dereferencing of crafted objects [eap-7.1.z] (CVE-2026-27727)\n\n* com.mchange/c3p0: c3p0: Arbitrary Code Execution via deserialization of\ncrafted objects [eap-7.1.z] (CVE-2026-27830)\n\n* netty-codec: Netty: Denial of Service via excessive memory allocation in\nLZ4FrameDecoder [eap-7.1.z] (CVE-2026-42583)\n\n* netty-handler-proxy: Netty: HTTP Header Injection via HttpProxyHandler Disabled Validation [eap-7.1.z] (CVE-2026-42578)\n\n* netty-codec-http: Netty: HTTP Request Smuggling due to improper handling\nof conflicting HTTP/1.0 headers [eap-7.1.z] (CVE-2026-42581)\n\n* netty-codec-http: Netty: Request smuggling via malformed\nTransfer-Encoding parsing [eap-7.1.z] (CVE-2026-42585)\n\n* netty-codec-http: Netty: Incorrect HTTP response parsing leads to data\nconfusion [eap-7.1.z] (CVE-2026-42584)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
